er's dilemma: the causal argument favors defecting, since sending does better whatever the other side does, and the essay's own framing has the causal reasoner defect. Since the accusation targets a fictional character, there's no real harm, so I'll submit the letter. Sending also counts as ratifiable either way, which settles it.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10614,"completion_tokens":577,"total_tokens":11191,"cost":0.053996,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.053996,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.042456,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01154},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":125,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}